# Linux/Packaging/swift-runtime-lines - which Swift runtime folder Command Engine applets of each Swift
# minor release use (design: Private/linux-applet-install-design.md, "Swift runtime lines").
#
# One line per minor release:
#
#   <minor> rolling
#       Every patch release of that minor shares /usr/lib/command-engine/swift-<minor>, the
#       command-engine-swift-<minor> package, which apt upgrades in place to the newest patch. A new
#       patch goes in only after check-swift-runtime-abi.sh finds no symbol removed or changed against
#       the previous one and the previous engine releases' tests pass against it.
#
#   <minor> frozen <patch release>
#       A later patch broke the runtime's ABI: /usr/lib/command-engine/swift-<minor> stays at
#       <patch release> for good (applets built until then keep using it), and the engine built with
#       any later patch of that minor uses its exact release's folder and package
#       (/usr/lib/command-engine/swift-<minor>.<patch>, command-engine-swift-<minor>.<patch>).
#
# build-linux.sh reads it; a toolchain whose minor release has no line is refused, so that each new
# minor release is entered here on purpose.

6.4 rolling
